  "kind": "statement",
  "title": "Open–closed weight devissage",
  "statement": "Let $j:U_0\\hookrightarrow X_0$ be open with closed complement\n$i:Z_0\\hookrightarrow X_0$. If the two outer terms\n$j_!j^*K$ and $i_*i^*K$ of the localization triangle\n$j_!j^*K\\to K\\to i_*i^*K\\to$ belong to $D_{\\le w}(X_0)$, then so\ndoes $K$.",
  "source": {
    "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-deligne-laumon-general/sk-l-dl-general-excision/lem-zl-open-closed-weight.md",
    "place": "node lem-zl-open-closed-weight, order 2815"
  },
  "stmt_deps": [
    "def-weil-complex-weights"
  ],
  "proof": [
    {
      "text": "The localization triangle is the open–closed recollement triangle of\n[def-weil-open-closed-recollement], which exists for $\\Qlb$-Weil complexes by [prop-sf-open-closed-triangle-all-stages]; by hypothesis its two outer\nterms lie in $D_{\\le w}(X_0)$, so the extension stability of complex\nweights [lem-zl-complex-extension] gives $K\\in D_{\\le w}(X_0)$.\n(The closed-immersion term $i_*i^*K$ is a finite-pushforward, hence\nhas the same weights as $i^*K$ by [lem-zl-finite-pushforward].)",
      "uses": [
        "def-weil-open-closed-recollement",
        "prop-sf-open-closed-triangle-all-stages",
        "lem-zl-complex-extension",
        "lem-zl-finite-pushforward"
      ],
      "elementary": false
    }
  ],
